  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜に{付|つ}け{込|こ}む: to take advantage of ~\n- {弱|よわ}みに{付|つ}け{込|こ}む: to exploit a weakness\n- {隙|すき}に{付|つ}け{込|こ}む: to exploit an opening\n- {善意|ぜんい}に{付|つ}け{込|こ}む: to take advantage of goodwill\n\nNOTE: Not to be confused with {漬|つ}け{込|こ}む (to pickle, to marinate), which is a homophone with a completely different meaning.",
